xt ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">needed</span><span id="lstnumberx58.269" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">.&lt;/</span><span id="lstnumberx58.270" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">task_context</span><span id="lstnumberx58.271" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&gt;\</span><span id="lstnumberx58.272" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">n</span><span id="lstnumberx58.273" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;/</span><span id="lstnumberx58.274" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">system</span><span id="lstnumberx58.275" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&gt;</span>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS9" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.9 </span>InjecAgent Additional Results</h3>

<div id="A1.SS9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">On GPT-4o, Enhanced attacks yield a lower baseline ASR (<math id="A1.SS9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3.5\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3.5</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.5\%</annotation></semantics></math>) than Base (<math id="A1.SS9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8.6\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>8.6</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8.6\%</annotation></semantics></math>), highlighting robustness to explicit instructions. Our defense halves ASR in both settings (to <math id="A1.SS9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4.3\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4.3</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4.3\%</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.1\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.1</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.1\%</annotation></semantics></math>), with strong protection against Data Stealing. <span id="A1.SS9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CommandSans</span>* excels in Enhanced attacks, while PI Detector proves brittle across variations. (see <a href="#A1.T11" title="In A.9 InjecAgent Additional Results ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ CommandSans: Securing AI Agents with Surgical Precision Prompt Sanitization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>)</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T11" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 11: </span>ASR (%) results on InjecAgent benchmark using GPT-4o. Our method reduces attack success across both Direct Harm and Data Stealing objectives, with strongest performance in Enhanced setting (<math id="A1.T11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.5</annotation></semantics></math>% → <math id="A1.T11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.1</annotation></semantics></math>% total ASR).</figcaption>
